Subject: Boot logo: built-in TacetOS logo, or the picture of the logo file

The firmware draws the built-in TacetOS logo before its disk is ready (on the
iPod Classic it keeps what the bootloader drew), then, once the disk is mounted,
what the logo file of the firmware folder asks for: the user's picture or a
black screen. A missing or damaged file leaves the TacetOS logo. No version
and no text at boot. The logo data is written by brand.sh.

